  "association": "Final cup geometry, dimensions, ties, floors and retention pads match the guarded CAD and actual-path records. Python stayed frozen during each native publication. The raw STEP/STL pair comes from the same two-cup print assembly at supplied placements; the delivered STL matches its completed TPU slice. After print export, only the separate inspection camera orientation and local path-review code changed; the printed geometry factory and print entry point stayed unchanged. Useful assembled/print views, annotated sections and actual-path detail were inspected. All four lid-pad contacts are intentional and limited to their 0.1mm bands. No success from the small L20 baseline or failed old M1/S16 liner is promoted to physical qualification of this tall application. Reviewed 2026-10-23: verification.py adds only the explicit rotary-l20-uniform route/declared choice; the historical rotary-l20 builder, checks, exports and slice are unchanged. This router-only association update does not transfer physical acceptance to the new revision."
